cument-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>EP</country><doc-number>0854134</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1092706A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIYOSHI HIDETAKA</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IHARA CHEMICAL IND CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KATSUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI SHUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIYOSHI, HIDETAKA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IHARA CHEMICAL INDUSTRY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KATSUNORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI, SHUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIYOSHI HIDETAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KATSUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI SHUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIYOSHI, HIDETAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KATSUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI, SHUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An easy and simple process for the preparation of phenylalkanoic acid amides having excellent germicidal activities; and intermediates therefor. Specifically, a process for the preparation of phenylalkanoic acid amides represented by general formula [3], (wherein X is hydrogen, alkyl, alkoxy, haloalkyl, or halogeno; n is an integer of 1 to 3, with the proviso that when n is 2 or above, Xs may be the same or different from each other; and Y and Z are each independently halogeno or hydrogen), characterized by reacting a carboxylic acid represented by general formula [1], (wherein X, n, Y and Z are each as defined above) with a dehydrating agent to form an oxazolinone represented by general formula [2], (wherein X, n, Y and Z are each as defined above), and reacting this oxazolinone with methyllithium or methylmagnesium halide.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé facile et simple pour l'élaboration d'amides d'acide phénylalcanoïque, qui ont d'excellents effets germicides, et des intermédiaires correspondants. Spécifiquement, l'invention concerne un procédé relatif à l'élaboration d'amides d'acide phénylalcanoïque de formule générale (3). Dans ladite formule, X est hydrogène, alkyle, alcoxy, haloalkyle ou halogéno; n est un entier valant entre 1 et 3, à condition que si n vaut 2 ou plus, les X peuvent être identiques ou différents; et Y et Z sont chacun indépendamment halogéno ou hydrogène. Ce procédé est caractérisé par la réaction entre un acide carboxylique de formule (1), dans laquelle X, n, Y et Z sont tels que définis ci-dessus, et un agent de déshydratation pour former une oxazolinone de formule générale (2), dans laquelle X, n, Y et Z sont tels que définis ci-dessus, et par la réaction entre cette oxazolinone et un halogénure de méthyllithium ou de méthylmagnésium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>